{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/1027","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/1027/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/1027/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/1027/events","html_url":"https://github.com/libgeos/geos/issues/1027","id":2080719437,"node_id":"I_kwDOACh1KM58BUJN","number":1027,"title":"ST_Covers gives incorrect answer after mutating POLYGON to MULTIPOLYGON","user":{"login":"cuteDen-ECNU","id":93959004,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZmzXA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93959004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cuteDen-ECNU","html_url":"https://github.com/cuteDen-ECNU","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cuteDen-ECNU/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cuteDen-ECNU/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cuteDen-ECNU/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cuteDen-ECNU/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cuteDen-ECNU/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cuteDen-ECNU/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cuteDen-ECNU/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cuteDen-ECNU/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cuteDen-ECNU/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1961427520,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTYxNDI3NTIw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/labels/Bug","name":"Bug","color":"d32304","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9425517018,"node_id":"LA_kwDOACh1KM8AAAACMc352g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/labels/Predicates","name":"Predicates","color":"c55ef3","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-14T13:00:08Z","updated_at":"2025-10-08T15:33:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Considering the following statement:\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT ST_Covers(g2, g1), ST_Covers(g3, g1) FROM\r\n(SELECT \r\nST_GeomFromText('GEOMETRYCOLLECTION ( LINESTRING (1 2, 1 1), POINT (0 0))') As g1\r\n, ST_GeomFromText(' MULTIPOLYGON (((0 0, 3 0, 3 3, 0 3, 0 0)))  ') As g2\r\n, ST_GeomFromText(' POLYGON ((0 0, 3 0, 3 3, 0 3, 0 0))  ') As g3\r\n);\r\n-- expected: {true, true}; actual: {false, true}\r\n```\r\nThe 2nd geometry covers the 1st one, because each point in the 1st geometry lies inside the 2nd one, according to the definition of ST_Covers:\r\n> ST_Covers(A, B) ⇔ A ⋂ B = B\r\n\r\nHowever, PostGIS doesn't consider the ST_Covers relation, which seems to be a bug. After normalizing MULTIPOLYGON to POLYGON as g3,  ST_Covers(g3, g1) gives the correct answer. \r\n\r\nHere is a simple reproduction for libgeos:\r\n```shell\r\nbin/geosop -a 'GEOMETRYCOLLECTION ( LINESTRING (1 2, 1 1), POINT (0 0))' -b 'MULTIPOLYGON (((0 0, 3 0, 3 3, 0 3, 0 0)))' covers\r\n# false\r\n```\r\ngeos version is the latest one in GitHub:\r\n6f70b63a0d976ce31dd2952094bc1a39209f8a20","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/1027/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/1027/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}